DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261231
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270101
SUMMARY:Deadline: A4 Residency Art Center: International Residency Fellowsh
 ip 2028 (Chengdu)
DESCRIPTION:The A4 Residency Art Center in Chengdu\, the residency platform
  of the A4 Art Museum in Luxelakes Eco-City\, opens its full-year 2028 rec
 ruitment.\n\nOrganisation: A4 Residency Art Center (A4 Art Museum)\nLocati
 on: Luxelakes Eco-City\, Tianfu New Area\, Chengdu\, China. Open worldwide
 .\nAward: Fully funded fellowship: private studio and accommodation\, roun
 d-trip economy airfare or second-class train ticket within a set budget\, 
 and a production grant of RMB 10\,000 per person/team for materials and pr
 oduction (excluding living expenses). No application fee.\nDuration: Appro
 ximately 8 weeks\, in the Spring 2028 (April to June) or Autumn 2028 (July
  to October) cycle.\n\nMore: https://www.a4artmuseum.com/en/a4-residencyar
 tcenter/residing/latest-recruitment/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk
 &utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.a4artmuseum.com/en/a4-residencyartcenter/residing/latest-re
 cruitment/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Luxelakes Eco-City\, Tianfu New Area\, Chengdu\, China. Open world
 wide.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:effea-call-5-festival-residencies-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T151252Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261103
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261104
SUMMARY:Deadline: EFFEA Call #5: European Festivals Fund for Emerging Artis
 ts
DESCRIPTION:The European Festivals Fund for Emerging Artists (EFFEA)\, an i
 nitiative of the European Festivals Association co-funded by the European 
 Union\, opens its fifth call: 50 residencies for 50 emerging artists (indi
 viduals\, groups or collectives) hosted by partnerships of around 150 fest
 ivals\, each led by one leading festival with a minimum of two partner fes
 tivals from different eligible countries.\n\nOrganisation: European Festiv
 als Association (EFA)\nLocation: Residencies hosted by festival partnershi
 ps of at least three festivals from three eligible countries (most of Euro
 pe plus Tunisia and Ukraine). Leading festivals and artists must be based 
 in an eligible country\; festivals from Israel\, Palestine\, Switzerland\,
  Turkey and the UK may join as partner festivals only\, and artists from t
 hose countries may also be proposed. Note: festivals apply\, proposing the
  artists\; artists cannot apply directly.\nAward: 50 residency grants: 40 
 Discovery grants of EUR 8\,000 (for artists at an early career stage) and 
 10 Springboard grants of EUR 15\,000 (for artists established at home and 
 ready to break through internationally). A minimum of 80 percent of the gr
 ant must cover costs incurred by the artists (fees\, travel\, accommodatio
 n\, subsistence). An own contribution of EUR 1\,000 (Discovery) or EUR 2\,
 000 (Springboard) is deducted from the paid grant. No application fee.\nDu
 ration: Residencies implemented between 1 January and 31 December 2027\, c
 o-produced by one leading festival and at least two partner festivals\n\nM
 ore: https://www.effea.eu/application-form?utm_source=artificialnouveaugra
 ntdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.effea.eu/application-form?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrant
 desk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Residencies hosted by festival partnerships of at least three fest
 ivals from three eligible countries (most of Europe plus Tunisia and Ukrai
 ne). Leading festivals and artists must be based in an eligible country\; 
 festivals from Israel\, Palestine\, Switzerland\, Turkey and the UK may jo
 in as partner festivals only\, and artists from those countries may also b
 e proposed. Note: festivals apply\, proposing the artists\; artists cannot
  apply directly.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:simons-foundation-open-interval-turbulence-2026@artificialnouveau.githu
 b.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T151252Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261021
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261022
SUMMARY:Deadline: Open Interval: An Artist-Scientist Exploration of Turbule
 nce
DESCRIPTION:Open Interval is a Simons Foundation program that supports trio
 s consisting of an artist\, a scientist\, and a representative from a 501(
 c)(3) arts organization to collaborate around a shared scientific theme. T
 he current cycle centers on the theme of turbulence\, a phenomenon at the 
 edge of chaos and beauty.\n\nOrganisation: Simons Foundation\nLocation: Un
 ited States (trio must be regionally co-located)\nAward: USD 30\,000 per a
 warded trio\nDuration: April to December 2027 (several months of collabora
 tion)\n\nMore: https://www.simonsfoundation.org/2026/06/01/coming-soon-ope
 n-interval-an-artist-scientist-exploration-of-turbulence/?utm_source=artif
 icialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.simonsfoundation.org/2026/06/01/coming-soon-open-interval-a
 n-artist-scientist-exploration-of-turbulence/?utm_source=artificialnouveau
 grantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:United States (trio must be regionally co-located)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:blackbird-foundation-believers-fund-iii-2026@artificialnouveau.github.i
 o
DTSTAMP:20261104T151252Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270630
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270701
SUMMARY:Deadline: Blackbird Foundation: Believers Fund III 2026
DESCRIPTION:Believers funds the people\, projects and programs creating the
  conditions for young people's creativity to flourish at scale. Creativity
  is meant in the broadest sense: artists are creative\, but so are scienti
 sts\, debaters\, community builders and dancers\, and a project can be any
 thing from a summer camp to a robotics competition to a co-working holiday
  house for artists.\n\nOrganisation: Blackbird Foundation\nLocation: Austr
 alia and/or New Zealand\; individuals\, groups or organisations establishe
 d in AU/NZ\, with projects taking place in AU/NZ.\nAward: AUD 5\,000 and A
 UD 10\,000 grants. No application fee.\nDuration: Projects must be complet
 ed within 12 months\n\nMore: https://www.blackbird.foundation/projects?utm
 _source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.blackbird.foundation/projects?utm_source=artificialnouveaug
 rantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Australia and/or New Zealand\; individuals\, groups or organisatio
 ns established in AU/NZ\, with projects taking place in AU/NZ.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:goethe-institut-aep-mobility-grants-2026-q2@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T151252Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261215
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261216
SUMMARY:Deadline: Goethe-Institut: Africa-Europe Mobility Grants (15 Decemb
 er 2026 Cut-Off)
DESCRIPTION:Sub-Saharan Component (Connect & Create) of the Africa-Europe P
 artnerships for Culture programme\, an EUR 8 million 42-month initiative (
 2025-2028) implemented by the Goethe-Institut in partnership with Expertis
 e France and Institut francais. PRIMARY FOCUS: transcontinental Africa-Afr
 ica short-term mobility for artists and culture professionals.\n\nOrganisa
 tion: Goethe-Institut (with Expertise France and Institut francais)\nLocat
 ion: Mobility within Sub-Saharan Africa (primary focus) and between Sub-Sa
 haran Africa and Europe\nAward: Up to EUR 4\,000 per mobility. Eligible co
 sts: travel (including visa and insurance)\, accommodation\, subsistence\,
  digital costs\, and top-up support for family\, disability\, and green mo
 bility. No application fee.\nDuration: Rolling call with quarterly cut-off
 s: 15 December 2026\, 15 March 2027\, 15 June 2027 and a final cut-off on 
 15 September 2027. Mobilities for the December cut-off take place between 
 1 January and 31 August 2027.\n\nMore: https://www.goethe.de/prj/aep/en/ca
 l/ssa/mga.html?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.goethe.de/prj/aep/en/cal/ssa/mga.html?utm_source=artificial
 nouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Mobility within Sub-Saharan Africa (primary focus) and between Sub
 -Saharan Africa and Europe
END:VEVENT
