DTSTAMP:20261104T151252Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261102
SUMMARY:Deadline: MIT Museum: BRAIN Digital Content Open Call
DESCRIPTION:The MIT Museum seeks proposals for compelling digital content e
 xploring humanity's relationship with the BRAIN\, the museum's thematic fo
 cus from April to September 2027 bringing together art\, science\, technol
 ogy and design on cognition\, neurotechnology\, brain-computer interfaces\
 , mental health and the boundaries of ability.\n\nOrganisation: MIT Museum
 \nLocation: Cambridge\, Massachusetts\, US (content shown on-site\; remote
  creation possible)\nAward: Flat honorarium of USD 2\,500 to 5\,000 per se
 lected proposal\, at the Museum's discretion\nDuration: BRAIN thematic foc
 us runs April - September 2027\; selection finalized January 2027\n\nMore:
  https://mitmuseum.mit.edu/brain-digital-content-open-call?utm_source=arti
 ficialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://mitmuseum.mit.edu/brain-digital-content-open-call?utm_source=ar
 tificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Cambridge\, Massachusetts\, US (content shown on-site\; remote cre
 ation possible)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:onx-seeds-soft-circuits-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T151252Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261026
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261027
SUMMARY:Deadline: Onassis ONX: ONX Seeds 2026\, Soft Circuits for Hard Time
 s (Athens\, hybrid)
DESCRIPTION:ONX Seeds 2026 is a four-month incubation and seed funding prog
 ram run by Onassis ONX\, the Onassis Foundation's platform for art and adv
 anced technologies\, hosted in Athens in a hybrid format under the theme S
 oft Circuits for Hard Times.\n\nOrganisation: Onassis ONX (Onassis Foundat
 ion)\nLocation: Athens\, Greece\, hybrid format. Open to creators from Gre
 ece and internationally\; remote participation for non-Athens teams.\nAwar
 d: EUR 1\,000 to 5\,000 seed funding per project\, set by scope\; up to fo
 ur projects selected. Plus weekly technical\, curatorial and business ment
 oring\, online masterclasses\, studio and equipment access at Onassis Read
 y for Athens-based teams\, and presentation at ONX Exhibition Athens (17 t
 o 21 March 2027) with travel\, accommodation and artwork transport covered
  for non-Athens participants. No application fee.\nDuration: Four-month in
 cubation\, culminating in ONX Exhibition Athens\, 17 to 21 March 2027.\n\n
 More: https://opencalls.onassis.org/onx-seeds-soft-circuits-for-hard-times
 -2?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://opencalls.onassis.org/onx-seeds-soft-circuits-for-hard-times-2?
 utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Athens\, Greece\, hybrid format. Open to creators from Greece and 
 internationally\; remote participation for non-Athens teams.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:make-a-thek-mobility-knowledge-exchange-2026@artificialnouveau.github.i
 o
DTSTAMP:20261104T151252Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261201
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261202
SUMMARY:Deadline: make-a-thek: Mobility Scheme & Knowledge Exchange Program
 me (Europe + pilot countries)
DESCRIPTION:make-a-thek\, a Horizon Europe project (grant No. 101177660) co
 ordinated by Fab Lab Barcelona at IAAC\, connects creative spaces\, public
  libraries and makers across Europe and beyond to share skills in circular
  fashion\, traditional crafts and technology. Its open call runs two track
 s.\n\nOrganisation: make-a-thek (coordinated by Fab Lab Barcelona at IAAC\
 , funded by Horizon Europe)\nLocation: Various European pilot cities (Antw
 erp\, Barcelona\, Berlin\, Budapest\, Helsinki\, Kranj\, Milan\, Opole\, R
 eykjavik\, Kyiv\, Zaporizhzhia)\; meet-ups in Barcelona (late Nov/early De
 c 2026) and Berlin (May 2027). Open to legal residents of EU member states
 \, Horizon Europe associated countries\, and the pilot countries Ghana\, S
 outh Africa\, Indonesia\, Philippines and Chile.\nAward: Mobility Scheme: 
 EUR 1\,000 flat stipend for experienced practitioners. Knowledge Exchange 
 Programme: EUR 850 flat stipend. Up to 12 participants per track annually.
  No application fee.\nDuration: Short-term mobility: single events\, works
 hops or 2-day group meet-ups (Barcelona between end of November and start 
 of December 2026\; Berlin in May 2027).\n\nMore: https://www.makeathek.eu/
 opencall?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.makeathek.eu/opencall?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk
 &utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Various European pilot cities (Antwerp\, Barcelona\, Berlin\, Buda
 pest\, Helsinki\, Kranj\, Milan\, Opole\, Reykjavik\, Kyiv\, Zaporizhzhia)
 \; meet-ups in Barcelona (late Nov/early Dec 2026) and Berlin (May 2027). 
 Open to legal residents of EU member states\, Horizon Europe associated co
 untries\, and the pilot countries Ghana\, South Africa\, Indonesia\, Phili
 ppines and Chile.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:culture-moves-europe-mobility-2026-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T151252Z
DTSTART:20270430T212900Z
DTEND:20270430T215900Z
SUMMARY:Deadline 23:59 CEST: Culture Moves Europe: Call for Individual Mobi
 lity 2026-2027
DESCRIPTION:Closes 30 Apr 2027 at 23:59 CEST.\n\nFlagship EU mobility grant
  for artists and cultural professionals: individual or group (up to 5 peop
 le) mobility to carry out an artistic or cultural project in another Creat
 ive Europe country\, with the support of an international partner of your 
 own choosing (an individual or an organisation). The project must follow 2
  of the 4 objectives: to learn\, to create\, to explore\, or to connect.\n
 \nOrganisation: Creative Europe (Culture Moves Europe)\, implemented by th
 e Goethe-Institut\nLocation: Creative Europe countries (incl. overseas cou
 ntries and territories and outermost regions)\; the project takes place in
  another Creative Europe country than your residence\nAward: EUR 85 per da
 y of project implementation\, plus travel allowance of EUR 400 (under 5\,0
 00 km) or EUR 800 (from 5\,000 km). Top-ups where applicable: green mobili
 ty EUR 400\, overseas countries and territories / outermost regions EUR 17
 5\, family EUR 200 per child under 18\, visa EUR 120. Accessibility suppor
 t: EUR 30 per day plus actual cost or fixed allowance for personal assista
 nce or sign language interpretation. No application fee.\nDuration: Projec
 t-based\n\nMore: https://culture.ec.europa.eu/culture-moves-europe/call-fo
 r-individual-mobility?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=ref
 erral
URL:https://culture.ec.europa.eu/culture-moves-europe/call-for-individual-m
 obility?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Creative Europe countries (incl. overseas countries and territorie
 s and outermost regions)\; the project takes place in another Creative Eur
 ope country than your residence
END:VEVENT
